      "marks": 5,
      "answer": "$k=3$ or $k=-\\frac{19}{7}$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Substitute $a=-\\frac72$ and rearrange: $4x^2-kx+\\frac12k^2=x+\\frac72$ — *M1; OE, all terms on one side, condone sign errors and watch multiples.\nUse $b^2-4ac$ with coefficients from their three-term quadratic: $(k+1)^2-16(\\frac12k^2-\\frac72)$ — *DM1; both $b,c$ must have two components.\n$7k^2-2k-57=0$ — A1; OE.\n$(k-3)(7k+19)=0$ or other valid solution method — DM1, dependent on both previous method marks.\n$k=3$ or $k=-\\frac{19}{7}$ — A1; OE, e.g. AWRT $-2.71$; no ISW if inequalities used. SC: if second DM1 not scored, SC B1 for correct final answers.\nAlternative: equate gradients $8x-k=1$ and curve/line, then form an equation in $x$ or $k$ — *M1 *DM1; obtain $28x^2-8x-3=0$ or $7k^2-2k-57=0$ — A1; solve — DM1; same answers — A1. Total: 5.",
